      "practice": "Abstracting and Generalizing",
      "why": "The item does not require the student to identify or extend a pattern beyond the given data, nor to generalize a rule or relationship across multiple cases. The task is to compare specific visual representations, not to derive or apply a broader principle about sampling or distributions."
    },
    {
      "practice": "Mathematical Modeling",
      "why": "There is no real-world scenario to be mathematized, no problem to be modeled, or solution to be checked for viability. The student is not creating or applying a model to represent a situation; they are simply comparing existing data representations."
    },
